---
import LPLayout from '../layouts/LPLayout.astro';
---

<LPLayout
	title="Refund & Course Rescheduling Policy | MicroDegree"
	description="MicroDegree refund policy, batch change and course rescheduling terms for learners."
	path="/refund-and-course-rescheduling-policy"
>
<div class="course-page text-center leading-normal font-poppins overflow-x-clip">
    <div class="relative p-4 min-h-screen">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto p-6 xl:shadow-lg 2xl:shadow-md lg:shadow-md md:shadow-md">
        <div class="flex flex-col justify-between leading-normal text-left">
          <div>

            
            <div class="w-full">
              <div class='flex items-center space-x-3'>
                <div class='bg-black p-[0.15rem] h-[0.2rem] w-[0.2rem] rounded-xl'></div> 
                <div class='bg-black p-[0.15rem] w-[0.1rem] rounded-xl'></div> 
                <p class='uppercase font-extrathin tracking-widest text-xs 2xl:text-[0.9rem]'>
                  <a href="https://www.microdegree.work/">Home</a> / Refund policy
                </p> 
                <div class='bg-black p-[0.15rem] h-[0.2rem] w-[0.2rem] rounded-xl'></div> 
                <div class='bg-black p-[0.15rem] h-[0.2rem] w-[0.2rem] rounded-xl'></div> 
              </div>

              <h1 class="font-semibold text-4xl mt-4 mb-10">
                Refund Policy
              </h1>
            </div>

            
            <div class='mb-16' id="intro">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                Welcome to MicroDegree!
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                Thank you for choosing to learn with us. These policies are designed to ensure clarity, fairness, and legal compliance for all learners. By enrolling in any MicroDegree program, you (the Learner) agree that these policies form part of your binding agreement with us, alongside our Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, and any enrollment-specific terms. Please read them carefully.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class='mb-5' id="everyone">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                1. Refund Policy
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                We want you to feel confident when joining MicroDegree. That’s why we’ve designed a simple and fair refund system, balancing student flexibility with the need to keep our programs sustainable for everyone.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class='mb-5' id="devops">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold my-5">
                Refund Timeline
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>100% Refund</span> – Request within 24 hours of payment</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>50% Refund</span> – If you cancel within 4 days of your batch start OR before attending 2 sessions (whichever comes first).</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>25% Refund</span> – If you cancel within 7 days of your batch start OR before attending 5 sessions (whichever comes first).</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>No Refund</span> – After 7 days from batch start OR once 5 sessions are completed (whichever comes first), as substantial course value would have already been delivered. This is subject, however, to the learner’s statutory rights under applicable consumer protection laws in cases of proven deficiency of service.</p></li>
              </ul>                                                          
            </div>

            <div class='mb-8' id="devops">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold my-5">
                Important Rules
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>To request a refund, write to us in our email: <a class='font-semibold' href="mailto:support@microdegree.work">support@microdegree.work</a> with the subject line: <span class='font-semibold'>“Refund Request – [Course Name]”</span> and attach your payment receipt.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Refunds will always be made to your original payment method within <span class='font-semibold'>14 working days</span> of approval.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Taxes and payment processing/gateway charges non-refundable.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Refunds are not applicable for discounted, promotional, or installment-based enrolments.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Refunds are not applicable for self-paced or recorded-only courses once access is granted to the learner.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Accessing class recordings, projects, or career resources will void the refund eligibility. </p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Duplicate payments, if any, will always be refunded in full within <span class='font-semibold'>10 working days</span>.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Refunds will not be provided for change of mind, lack of use, or failure to attend. </p></li>
              </ul>                                                          
            </div>

                        <div class='mb-16' id="devops">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold my-5">
                Access Misuse:
              </h3>
              <p class='text-base mb-5 ml-3'>If at any time it is found that the learner has:</p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>shared course access with multiple users,</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>copied, downloaded, or attempted to replicate course content for redistribution, or</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>used the program with the intention of copying materials,</p></li>
              </ul>
               <p class='text-base mb-2 ml-3'>MicroDegree reserves the right to immediately revoke access without refund, and may take action under the Intellectual Property Rights clause of this Policy.</p>                                                       
            </div>

            <div class='mb-16' id="plan2">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                2. Plan Change Policy
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                We understand that learning needs can change. Here’s how plan changes work:
              </p>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                Any requests for plan change will be processed within 7 working days.
              </p>

              <p class="text-xl leading-8 my-5 font-semibold">
                In case of: 
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>Upgrade:</span> Allowed within 30 days of payment. The learner must pay the full difference between standard course prices (not just the discounted gap). <span class='font-semibold'>E.g.</span> If the fees of Course A is ₹30,000 (you bought at ₹28,000 discount) and Course B is ₹40,000, you must pay full ₹10,000 to change to Course B. Paying only the discounted gap amount will not be approved. An upgrade to new course will not be made at discount, unless there is a specific offer/promotional condition to this effect.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>Downgrade:</span> Allowed within <span class='font-semibold'>7 days</span> of batch start, with refund of the difference (minus gateway charges). No downgrades will be allowed after the 7 days period. Further, downgrade to a different course is not offered for partial payments, EMIs, discounted payments, and/or promotional offers.</p></li>
              </ul>                                                          
            </div>

            <div class='mb-16' id="devops">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                3. Batch & Trainer Change Policy
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                A batch change means moving to a different scheduled cohort (weekday ↔ weekend, morning ↔ evening) for the same course.
              </p>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 font-semibold">
                * If MicroDegree reschedules a batch, the change will be free.
              </p>

              <p class="text-xl leading-8 my-5 font-semibold">
                Batch change fee/structure in case of voluntary changes:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>1st change → Free</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>2nd change → ₹2,000</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>3rd change → ₹10,000</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>4th change → New enrollment required</p></li>
              </ul>
              <p class="text-xl leading-8 my-5 font-semibold">
                Guidelines:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Maximum <span class='font-semibold'>3 batch changes</span> per course in 1 year (4th requires new enrollment).</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Trainer preference requests will be considered where possible. but final allocation shall depend on batch schedules and availability.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Batch change applies to only in one course in your career path that you have chosen and paid up for (e.g., in AWS or DevOps). In case of Course change, <a onClick={() => {document.getElementById('plan2')?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });}} 
        class="underline font-semibold">please refer to Plan change Policy at 2.</a></p></li>
              </ul> 

              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5" id="plan4">
                4. Course Access & Validity
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Standard access: 1 year from batch start date.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Recording extension: ₹999 + taxes per year.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Temporary downtime → access restored promptly.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Platform closure → no refunds, but materials will be provided.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-16'>Rejoining after 1 year requires re-enrollment at current prices.</p></li>
              </ul>   

                            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                5. Career Assistance & Placement Terms
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>At MicroDegree, our mission is to guide you to a successful Cloud & DevOps career.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>We provide training, career prep sessions, resume reviews, mock interviews, and interview opportunities, but your effort is the key factor.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Each learner shall receive one year of career assistance from the start of their batch. This includes weekly career prep sessions, mock tests, mock interviews, weekend technical interview prep, resume reviews, and curated job alerts with interview opportunities.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Learners are assured a minimum number of interview opportunities based on their plan: 1–3 interviews for Freshers/Non-IT to IT plans, and 5–12+ interviews for IT Professional plans. These are provided only if the learner meets <span class='font-semibold'>readiness criteria</span> and if suitable roles exist in prevailing relevant job market conditions, and/or relevant openings are verified by MicroDegree’s placement team.</p></li>
              </ul>                                        
                          <p class="text-xl leading-8 my-5 font-semibold">
                To qualify for placement assistance, learner must:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Comply with the “readiness criteria” (i.e. ≥75% attendance, completion of all assignments, and ≥60% score in mock assessments.)</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Participate in mock tests & mock interviews</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Submit resumes for approval and implement suggested improvements</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Attempt and clear the Placement Drive (<span class='font-semibold'>held twice a month</span>)</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Actively apply to job opportunities shared by MicroDegree</p></li> 
                <li><p class='mb-5'>MicroDegree may, at its discretion, relax the eligibility criteria in cases where a learner demonstrates genuine effort and readiness, even if minor shortfalls exist.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Job offers are made by third-party employers, who retain sole discretion over hiring decisions.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>MicroDegree is not responsible for withdrawal, modification, or non-issuance of job offers by employers.</p></li>
              </ul>
 <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                6. Intellectual Property Rights (IPR)
              </h3>
                            <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>All course materials are the intellectual property of MicroDegree Education Private Limited.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>As a learner, you shall receive a limited, non-transferable license for personal educational use. (For Access timeline, <a onClick={() => {document.getElementById('plan4')?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });}} 
        class="underline font-semibold">please refer to Plan change Policy at 4.</a>).</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Unauthorized copying, sharing, resale, or reproduction of MicroDegree’s proprietary course materials is prohibited.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Violation will result in immediate termination without refund, and MicroDegree shall have every right to initiate criminal action under <span class='font-semibold'>relevant IPR laws</span> and/or <span class='font-semibold'>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita</span> (BNS), and/or civil action in the form of including court orders to stop misuse, or seek compensation if its intellectual property rights are violated,  or are at risk of violation, before the appropriate court within the territory of India.</p></li>
              </ul> 
                                        
    <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                7. Indemnity & Limitation of Liability
              </h3>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                Learners agree to indemnify and hold harmless MicroDegree against any claims, damages, or expenses arising from:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Violation of these policies or applicable law.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Misuse or unauthorized distribution of course materials.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Infringement of third-party rights.</p></li>
              </ul>  
                                        <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
                <span class='font-semibold'>Limitation of Liability:</span> MicroDegree’s total liability is limited to the amount paid by the learner for the course.
              </p>


    <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                8. Force Majeure
              </h3>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
                In rare cases where classes are postponed due to events outside our control (e.g., natural disasters, political disruptions, or technical failures), MicroDegree will reschedule sessions at no extra cost, and learners will retain access to course recordings and materials.
              </p>

              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                9. Dispute Resolution & Governing Law
              </h3>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                <span class='font-semibold'>Grievance Redressal Mechanism:</span> In compliance with the <span class='font-semibold'>Consumer Protection Act, 2019</span> and <span class='font-semibold'>the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules, 2020</span>, MicroDegree has appointed a Grievance Officer, given here below:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-10 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>Name: [To be filled by company]</span></p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>Email: [To be filled by company]</span></p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>Contact No.: [To be filled by company]</span></p></li>
              </ul>

              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Any learner grievances should first be addressed to the Grievance Officer. A written response will be provided within <span class='font-semibold'>14 working days</span>.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>For minor grievances or operational issues (such as access difficulties, scheduling clarifications, or payment status queries), learners are encouraged to first contact MicroDegree’s support team at <a class='font-semibold' href="mailto:support@microdegree.work">support@microdegree.work</a>. MicroDegree will make every reasonable effort to resolve such matters promptly through mutual discussion, system corrections, or other amicable solutions.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Learners agree that unresolved grievances shall first be referred to sole arbitration under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996. Proceedings shall be in English, confidential, and held in Mangalore, Karnataka (or virtually, at MicroDegree’s or the arbitrator’s discretion). The arbitral award shall be final and binding, and courts at Mangalore shall have exclusive jurisdiction for enforcement or interim relief.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>This clause constitutes an “arbitration agreement” under Section 7 of the Act. Learners further agree to first exhaust the grievance redressal mechanism and attempt resolution through arbitration before initiating proceedings under the <span class='font-semibold'>Consumer Protection Act, 2019</span>, except where urgent statutory relief is available from a Consumer Commission.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Nothing in this clause shall restrict a learner’s statutory rights under the <span class='font-semibold'>Consumer Protection Act, 2019</span>. Should a learner approach a Consumer Commission, MicroDegree may request that the matter be referred to arbitration in accordance with this clause.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>This Policy shall be governed by the laws of India.</p></li>
              </ul> 

              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                10. Policy Updates & Version Control
              </h3>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
               This policy may be revised from time to time to reflect changes in MicroDegree’s services, operations, or applicable laws. MicroDegree reserves the right to amend, modify, or update this policy as and when required, provided that such changes remain consistent with applicable legal requirements. Learners will be notified of any material updates through their registered email address and/or via notifications on the student dashboard, and the most recent version will always be available for review on the student dashboard. For each learner, the version of the policy applicable will be the one in force on the date of enrollment, unless a later update is required by law or regulatory compliance, in which case the updated version shall apply. By continuing to use MicroDegree’s services after such updates, learners are deemed to have read, understood, and agreed to the revised policy.
              </p>

<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                11. Termination of Services
              </h3>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
                MicroDegree reserves the right to suspend or terminate learner access in cases of:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-10 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Non-payment of fees.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Breach of this policy or Terms of Use.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Any kind of misconduct towards staff or peers.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>IPR or ethical violations.</p></li>
              </ul>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
                Termination will usually follow a written warning, except in severe breaches (e.g., IPR violation such as resale of content), where termination will be immediate
              </p>

              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                12. Age & Eligibility
              </h3>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
               By enrolling, you confirm that you are at least 18 years of age, or in case you are a minor (below the age of 18), you are enrolling with parental/guardian consent, who shall be jointly responsible for compliance with this policy.
              </p>
<p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
               By permitting the minor to enroll/access the paid recorded materials, the parent/guardian accepts full responsibility for: (i) all obligations of the learner under this Policy, (ii) ensuring compliance with its terms, and (iii) any consequences of misuse or breach. MicroDegree reserves the right to seek confirmation of such consent at any time.
              </p>

               <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                13. Confidentiality & Data Sharing for Placements
              </h3>
                            <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Learner data will be handled in accordance with the Privacy Policy.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>MicroDegree follows the <span class='font-semibold'>Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023</span>. Learner data is used only for training and career support, kept only as long as needed or legally required, and can be deleted on request after course completion (subject to applicable laws).</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Resumes will only be shared with verified employer-partners for placement purposes.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Consent will be obtained before data is shared.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>MicroDegree will not sell learner data to unrelated third parties.</p></li>
              </ul>

 <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                14. Disclaimer of Warranties
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
               Courses and services are provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis. MicroDegree does not warrant that:
              </p>
                <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Training will guarantee employment.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>The platform will be uninterrupted or error-free.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Outcomes will meet individual expectations.</p></li>
              </ul> 

 <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                15. Enforcement Procedure
              </h3>
                <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-16 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>For minor breaches (e.g., accidental sharing), a written warning will be issued.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>For serious breaches (e.g., fraud, resale), MicroDegree may immediately revoke access without refund and take legal action.</p></li>
              </ul> 

 <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                16. Severability & Entire Agreement
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
               If any provision of this policy is held invalid, the remainder shall continue in effect. This policy, along with the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy, constitutes the entire agreement between the learner and MicroDegree.
              </p>

 <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                17. Severability & Entire Agreement
              </h3>
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5 mb-16">
               This policy may be translated into regional languages for convenience. In case of conflict, the English version shall prevail.
              </p>

 <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold my-5">
                Key Takeaways (Student-Friendly Summary)
              </h3>
                <ul class="list-disc text-base mb-2 ml-3">
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Flexible, fair refund system (time + session-based).</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Refunds processed only via original payment method.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Batch/plan changes allowed within clear limits.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>1-year access with extensions available.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>1-year structured career assistance with mock interviews & drives</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Interview opportunities require active participation</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'>Career assistance with clear eligibility rules.</p></li>
                <li><p class='mb-5'><span class='font-semibold'>No job/placement guarantee. Outcomes depend on student readiness and market conditions.</span></p></li>
              </ul> 
              <p class="text-base leading-8 my-5">
               This policy is issued by MicroDegree Education Private Limited and is binding on all learners. By enrolling, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to the terms set out above.
              </p>

            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
</div>
</LPLayout>

<style is:global>
	/* The old app wrapped pages in .App { text-align: center } and loaded App.css; the layout of these pages depends on both. */
	.course-page .container { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; padding: 5px; }
</style>
